-- title:
--   Divisibility of y-y(v) by z-z(v) at a simple point
-- statement:
--   Let $K \subseteq F$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra, and let $v$ be a place of $F$ over $K$, that is, a valuation subring $\mathcal O_v =$ `v.toValuationSubring` of $F$ which contains $\mathrm{image}$ of $K$ under the structure map, is not all of $F$, and is a principal ideal ring. Assume $v$ is rational, i.e. the composite $K \to \mathcal O_v \to \mathcal O_v/\mathfrak m_v$ into the residue field is surjective, so that the evaluation map $f \mapsto f(v) :=$ `v.evalAt f`, sending $f \in \mathcal O_v$ to a chosen preimage in $K$ of the residue of $f$ (and everything outside $\mathcal O_v$ to $0$), is defined. Let $z, y \in \mathcal O_v$ and let $G \in K[X][Y]$ be a polynomial in one variable over $K[X]$. Suppose that $G$, with its coefficients mapped into $F[X][Y]$, vanishes at $(z,y)$, in the sense that substituting $z$ for the inner variable and $y$ for the outer one gives $0$ in $F$; and suppose that the derivative of $G$ with respect to the outer variable, evaluated in $K$ at the inner value $z(v)$ and the outer value $y(v)$, is nonzero. Then there exists $h \in \mathcal O_v$ with $y - y(v) = h\,(z - z(v))$ in $F$, the values $y(v), z(v) \in K$ being viewed in $F$.
--
--   This is the implicit-function (Hensel) step at a simple point of a plane relation $G(z,y)=0$: in the valuation ring of a rational place, $y-y(v)$ lies in the ideal generated by $z-z(v)$ as soon as $\partial G/\partial Y$ does not vanish at the point $(z(v),y(v))$. It is used to show that $z-z(v)$ is a uniformiser at $v$ once $y-y(v)$ is known to be one, in [`AlgebraicCurve.Place.ord_sub_algebraMap_evalAt_eq_one_of_derivative_evalEval_ne_zero_of_ord_sub_algebraMap_evalAt_eq_one`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.Place.ord_sub_algebraMap_evalAt_eq_one_of_derivative_evalEval_ne_zero_of_ord_sub_algebraMap_evalAt_eq_one).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_Place_exists_sub_algebraMap_evalAt_eq_mul_of_derivative_evalEval_ne_zero.lean

